OL,3,GNEWSAResidents urged to have say on
OL,4,Aborough's future
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents have been urged to have their
OL,7,Fsay after the launch of a consultation
OL,8,Fon the future of development in their
OL,9,Fborough.
OL,11,FThurrock Council has published its
OL,12,Fdraft local plan, setting out where
OL,13,Ffuture homes, jobs, infrastructure and
OL,14,Fcommunity facilities are going to be
OL,15,Flocated over the next two decades.
OL,17,FIt has invited the public to have their
OL,18,Fsay on the proposals, including a
OL,19,Fseries of drop-in events during the
OL,20,Fconsultation period, which runs until
OL,21,F14 November.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
